// The cobbles themselves, one instanced mesh for the lot. Along a path they're laid in rows
// across it; a round landing gets rings of them round a middle stone. Where two paths overlap
// the stones are set one path at a time, landings first, then the rings, then the rest, and a
// stone that would run into one already set is cut down to meet it, so the paths join flush.
